1. The stratospheric ozone umbrella absorbs more than 98% of harmful, high-energy solar ultraviolet radiation (UV-B and UV-C).
2. If the ozone shield were depleted, intense UV radiation would reach Earth's surface with catastrophic biological impacts:
   (a) **Severe Human Health Damage**: Widespread incidence of malignant skin melanoma, corneal cataracts, blindness, and immunosuppression;
   (b) **Destruction of Marine Food Webs**: UV radiation penetrates shallow ocean water, killing microscopic phytoplankton (which produce 50% of planetary oxygen and form the foundational base of all marine food chains);
   (c) **Agricultural Collapse**: UV radiation damages plant chlorophyll and cellular DNA, stunting crop growth, mutating pollen, and slashing global agricultural yields.
